{
  "The appointment form set up without events: which fields, in which order, in groups and tabs; editors of your own; checks per field; fields shown or locked for one appointment only. Or a form of your own.": "",
  "Items, groups and tabs": "",
  "`editing.form.items` lists what the form holds. A built-in item and a resource are named by their fields; an item with the same `field` changes that one (here the title's label and a rule). The time zone row (`timeZone`) and the recurrence editor (`recurrenceRule`) are items like the others: move them, or leave them out. `tabs` and groups hold items named the same way.": "",
  "Editors of your own": "",
  "`editor` may be a function: it gets the props a named editor gets (`label`, `value`, `onValueChanged`, `validationGroup`, `rules` …), so any component that takes them is checked with the form. `template` places any MotifJS component; it gets the form (its reactive `data`) and its place (`field`, `validationGroup`). `rules` are the kit's validation rules, added to a built-in's own.": "",
  "Fields for one appointment": "",
  "`visible`, `readOnly`, `enabled`, `required`, `label` and `helpText` may be functions of the form: `(form) => form.data.roomId === 3`. They read the form's data as it is now, so a field shows when another changes.": "",
  "A form of your own": "",
  "`onFormOpening` gets the items `editing.form` made and may still change them; `cancel` keeps the scheduler's form closed. Open your own, then save with `addAppointment` or `updateAppointment`: the events and the checks run as for the scheduler's form.": "",
  "editing.form": "",
  "the built-ins, the resources after All day": "",
  "What the form holds, in order: a built-in item by its field, a resource by its field, or an item of your own. Unknown names are left out.": "",
  "Columns of the form (a group and a tab may have their own).": "",
  "With it, as many columns as fit, each at least this wide; `columns` is the most.": "",
  "New / Edit appointment": "",
  "The form’s title; a function of the form may say it per appointment.": "",
  "The form’s width, a CSS length.": "",
  "Built-in items": "",
  "Name": "",
  "The title (required) and the description.": "",
  "Each two items: a date and time, and (all day) a date. The end checks it is after the start and that the time is free.": "",
  "The all-day switch.": "",
  "The time zone row: `startTimeZone`, `separateEndZone`, `endTimeZone` (with `editing.allowTimeZones`), each may be named alone too.": "",
  "The recurrence editor (with `editing.allowRecurrence`).": "",
  "Its picker: a drop-down, or a tag box for a kind of several; each item with its colour.": "",
  "SchedulerFormItem": "",
  "As a kit form item. `editor` may be a name or a function that makes the editor from the props a named one gets.": "",
  "A value, a function that is followed, or a function of the form `(form) => …` (its `appointment`, `data`, `isNew`): shown or locked for one appointment only.": "",
  "Kit validation rules (or a function of the form giving them); added to a built-in’s own.": "",
  "A group under a caption, its items named or given the same way.": "",
  "`[{ title, items, columns?, visible? }]`: tabs, every tab checked when the form is saved; the tab of the first field that failed shows.": "",
  "`(form, place) => ComponentBase`: any MotifJS component for this place; `place` has the `field` and the `validationGroup` to check it with the others.": "",
  "A button of the form.": "",
  "How they combine": "",
  "Its settings win; `rules` add; `visible` and `enabled` hold when both say so; `readOnly` when either does; `editorProps` merge.": "",
